{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a426bb90-8d08-47d0-b0e1-0c739d1c410b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Fixed prompt caching by splitting the system prompt in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-RlReO2/bot.py) into two distinct cached segments. Documented the changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-RlReO2/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Split `build_system` in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-RlReO2/bot.py#L130-L138)**:\n   - Previously, the system prompt was sent as a single combined block with one `cache_control` marker, causing any change to athlete facts to invalidate the entire cache including static instructions.\n   - Now returns two text blocks, each with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n     - **Block 1 (Static Prefix)**: `INSTRUCTIONS` (~780 tokens) byte-identical across all users and dates.\n     - **Block 2 (Volatile Tail)**: `athlete_context(a, today)` (~240 tokens: date, athlete profile, zones, goal, facts, language).\n\n2. **Impact**:\n   - Calling `save_fact` only invalidates the volatile tail (~240 tokens) on subsequent calls while the static instruction prefix stays hot in cache.\n","duration_seconds":54.389038,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":112597,"output_tokens":1711,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":150146,"total_tokens":114308}}}
